invariant: INV-26
file: Makefile
catches: test/lint-trust-separation.sh
reason: AES=hw stops packaging ghash_hw.c, so an AES=hw object
  carries aes_hw.c and a gcm.c that calls two GHASH entries no
  source in the object defines. A linker would refuse the test binaries,
  but a linker is not the gate: it names a missing symbol, not the axis
  value that lost its source, and a firmware tree that copies the
  source list from here would meet the error in its own build. The lint
  reads the packaged source list per axis value, and its AES=hw row
  requires both AES=hw sources.

--- old
AES_HW_SRCS := aes_hw.c ghash_hw.c
--- new
AES_HW_SRCS := aes_hw.c
